# Sequential section numbering (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-17), verbatim:

> **Hard rule: Always check all documents for sequential section
> completeness (no gaps in number/lettering) system. This is a
> mistake you made from extracting sections, but not renumbering
> them.**

## The rule

> **After any insert, extract, delete, or move of a numbered or
> lettered section, renumber the entire remaining outline so
> Article, Section, and Schedule identifiers are consecutive.
> Do not leave a hole because a section was removed.**

Consecutive means 1, 2, 3 ...; 1.1, 1.2, 1.3 ...; A, B, C ...;
and 4.15.1, 4.15.2 ... at the same level. A retired letter is
not a reserved hole. Close the sequence.

## Scope

Applies to Go-to-Market (GTM) contracts under
`pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/contracts/` and to any other
structured document the agent authors or edits (agreements,
schedules, Non-Disclosure Agreements (NDAs), End User License
Agreement (EULA), READMEs with numbered articles). Always check
before render or commit.

## Forbidden

- Leaving a hole (4.14 then 4.16; Schedule D then Schedule F;
  3.2 then 3.4) because a section was extracted or deleted
- Inventing a new section only to fill a hole
- Updating headings but leaving "as stated in Section 4.9" pointing
  at the wrong clause
- Coined labels such as lane or band in examples or new headings

## Required agent behavior

1. After an outline edit, renumber remaining sections at every
   affected level.
2. Update every internal cross-reference, fee-table pointer,
   survival list, and renderer `pdf_inspect` marker in the same
   change set.
3. Before render or commit of a contract, scan for skipped
   integers and skipped schedule letters.
4. Do not invent legal terms
   ([`standard-legal-terminology.mdc`](standard-legal-terminology.mdc)).
   Do not insert LLM sidenotes
   ([`no-llm-sidenotes-in-contracts.mdc`](no-llm-sidenotes-in-contracts.mdc)).

## Worked violation to fix

**Violation** (extract without closing the sequence):

```text
### 4.14 Services Revenue Split
### 4.16 MSP Resale
## SCHEDULE D - DEAL REGISTRATION
## SCHEDULE F - COMPENSATION
```

Section 4.15 and Schedule E were removed. The leftover numbers
and letters kept the holes.

**Fix** (renumber what remains; update cites):

```text
### 4.14 Services Revenue Split
### 4.15 MSP Resale
## SCHEDULE D - DEAL REGISTRATION
## SCHEDULE E - COMPENSATION
```

Every "Section 4.16" and "Schedule F" cite follows the new
identifier. Legal meaning is unchanged.

## Origin

2026-09-17 - operator hard rule after section extraction without
renumbering. Always check sequential completeness; close gaps;
update cross-references in the same change set.
